    10	## Validation at execute time
    11	
    12	- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16)).
    13	- A missing required property is rejected before the executor is invoked ([validated by: rejects missing required input before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6)).
    14	- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: names the field and expected type when rejecting a wrong-typed property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L37), [validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
    15	- When `input` supplies a value outside a declared `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a rejection naming the field path and enum constraint without including the value.
    16	- A nested type failure names its property path using dot notation ([validated by: reports nested property paths in validation rejections](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L46)).
    17	- A top-level type failure names its property path without a leading punctuation character ([validated by: does not prefix top-level validation paths with punctuation](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L65)).
    18	- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input and undeclared properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L23)).
    19	- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
    20	
    21	## Schema compilation and caching
    22	
    23	- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
    24	- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses a static schema validator across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L74)).
    25	- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.
    26	
    27	## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
    28	
    29	- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
